{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["The reason for <b>עֲוֹנָה בָהּ</b> — \"at the time when her iniquity is upon her,\" and not at the time when she has repented; this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Numbers 15:31), from the words of our Sages (Shevuot 13). And according to the plain sense of Scripture it is like \"their blood is upon them\" (Leviticus 20:27), \"they shall bear their sin: they shall die childless\" (ibid. verse 20), \"he has uncovered his sister's nakedness; he shall bear his iniquity\" (ibid. verse 17). And I saw in Pirkei DeRabbi Eliezer: What is the meaning of \"her iniquity is upon her\"? It teaches that the soul is sold and its iniquity is with it — that is to say, that the transgression clings to it after excision (karet), so that it is judged with punishments forever, in the manner of \"for their worm shall not die, nor shall their fire be quenched\" (Isaiah 66:24)."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:05:50.917806753Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}